The H R F and convolution.

5
00:00:16,723 --> 00:00:24,923
The hemodynamic response function (H R F) approximates the delayed, smooth bold response that follows brief neural activity.

6
00:00:24,923 --> 00:00:30,846
Convolution combines event timing with this response shape to create a model predictor.

7
00:00:30,846 --> 00:00:37,680
The predictor should resemble the signal you expect to measure, not an instantaneous event list.

8
00:00:37,680 --> 00:00:44,515
FEAT offers basis choices and temporal derivatives, but extra flexibility changes the model and interpretation.

